statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:a4afb9a6a45e031f3e8ed0a3483675bb211523829f7813592b4a5da69045a206","file":"preprints/Finite-Circle-Obstructions-Binary-Codes-and-Histogram-Embeddings-for-Edit-Distance-September-27-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":28,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"bc355747e8872f91559ddaeaf06c0c04cc274c66b26f9ad39dcc7b65f0e710c2","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Finite-Circle-Obstructions-Binary-Codes-and-Histogram-Embeddings-for-Edit-Distance-September-27-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:a4afb9a6a45e031f3e8ed0a3483675bb211523829f7813592b4a5da69045a206","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Finite-Circle-Obstructions-Binary-Codes-and-Histogram-Embeddings-for-Edit-Distance-September-27-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L28"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere are absolute constants $c,C>0$ and an integer $d_0$ such that, for\nevery integer $d\\geq d_0$ and every finite alphabet $\\Sigma$ with\n$|\\Sigma|\\geq2$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:main}\n \\exp\\!\\bigl(c\\sqrt{\\log d\\,\\log\\log d}\\bigr)\n \\leq E_\\Sigma(d)\\leq\n \\exp\\!\\bigl(C\\sqrt{\\log d\\,\\log\\log d}\\bigr).\n\\end{equation}\nEach of our two lower constructions supplies a binary subset whose words\nhave one common length at most $d$ and whose least $\\ell_1$ distortion\nsatisfies the lower bound. The upper bound is realized by a deterministic\nfinite-dimensional map."}
